      ],
      "depiction": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/docs/cat-harness/assets/img/workflows/actor-role-administration.svg",
      "description": "Changing who can do what: adding an actor, opening or closing a role to one, granting or revoking a permission — and auditing the graph afterwards, because the declaration and the graph are two things that can disagree.\n\nYou are in this process when the substrate every other diagram's lanes bind to is what is changing. That is why it is drawn rather than left as a filesystem edit: a role added without an audit is a lane binding that resolves today and may not tomorrow, and nothing else in the corpus would notice.\n\nRetirement, never deletion. An actor id is referenced from commits, sidecars and other declarations, so removing one makes an old record unreadable while retiring one leaves it legible and says the actor has stopped.",
      "enforcement": "strict",
      "flowCount": 14,
      "inSubgraph": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness.jsonld#directory/processes",
      "name": "Actor and role administration",
      "nodeCount": 11,
